  "location": "CRE54.8 bullet 1 (reference to CRE22.61)",
  "text": {
    "en": {
      "title": "Basel Framework: CRE54.8 bullet 1 (reference to CRE22.61)",
      "summary": "CRE54.8 points to CRE22.61 for the 20-day MPOR floor on netting sets above 5000 trades, but that floor is in CRE22.58.",
      "impact": "Position: Banks using the comprehensive approach, SFT netting set with 6000 trades, no illiquid collateral, no disputes, cleared at a QCCP Reading a: Follow the pointer literally: CRE22.61 contains no floor, so for the SFT leg the disapplication in CRE54.8 has nothing to disapply and the reader must guess the holding period Reading b: Read CRE22.58 by intent: 20-day floor disapplied, holding period 5 business days (repo-style, CRE22.57) Difference: Holding period 20 vs 5 business days under a literal reading of CRE22.58 without the CCP exception; sqrt scaling of haircuts about x2",
      "correction": "Clarify or correct the cited passage so that the rule and its references give one result for the stated case."
    }
  },
